                <pb facs="0962" n="952" sameAs="frus:frus1949v08/pg952"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">125.633/4–1549: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Consul General at Peiping</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Clubb</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1949-04-15T19:00:00-05:00">April 15, 1949—7
                            p. m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>213. Immediately following tel<anchor n="42" xml:id="d1166-f1"/> requests you
                    make further approach Commies re Mukden. If you feel recent joint approach you
                    and ur colleagues re consular facilities Peiping (urtel 611 Apr 14<anchor n="43"
                        xml:id="d1166-f2"/>) makes desirable deferring Mukden issue few days or a
                    week Dept would have no objection thereto but desires be informed thereof.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Acheson</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
